"program_narrative": "BCHCTL00 is a called batch-control subprogram (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LS-CONTROL-REQUEST) that is meant to manage a job's record in the indexed BATCH-CONTROL-FILE (layout from copybook BCHCTL, keyed by BCT-KEY). The caller selects one of four functions in LS-FUNCTION: 'INIT' (open files, read and validate the control record, mark the job started), 'CHEK' (read the control record and check its dependencies, returning BCT-RC-SUCCESS 0 when prerequisites are satisfied and BCT-RC-WARNING 4 otherwise), 'UPDT' (read, update and write the control record) and 'TERM' (record completion and close files). Each function first sets an internal process-mode flag; an unrecognised function sets ERR-TEXT, returns BCT-RC-ERROR 8 and calls the common error processor ERRPROC. In every case the program then copies LS-RETURN-CODE to RETURN-CODE and returns with GOBACK. All 11 detail paragraphs that would perform the file work are not present in the source (a trailing comment marks most of them 'to be implemented'), so only the dispatch and return-code logic can be traced.",
